- Switch: `<input type="checkbox" role="switch" checked>` 
- Checkbox: `<input type="checkbox" checked>`
- Button: `<button type="button" aria-pressed="true|false">text</button>`

Let me check how `f32_property` works and whether the value_type matters. From the SLIDER code: `node.f32_property(property_id::MIN_VALUE, 0.0)` — reads the property value as f32. For TOGGLE_STYLE (F32 enum code), f32_property(TOGGLE_STYLE, 0.0) returns the enum code as f32. Then `round()` to compare.

Let me check the `f32_property` helper signature — need to confirm it exists and how it handles missing (default). From SLIDER usage: `node.f32_property(property_id::MIN_VALUE, 0.0)`. Good.

New TOGGLE arm:
```rust
component_type::TOGGLE => {
    let style = node.f32_property(property_id::TOGGLE_STYLE, 0.0).round() as u8;
    let checked = node.checked();
    let text = escape(node.text.as_deref().unwrap_or_default());
    let style_attr = style_attr(&border);
    match style {
        1 => format!(
            "<label{data_id} class=\"pathland-toggle\"{style_attr}><input type=\"checkbox\"{checked}{sep}><span class=\"pathland-text\">{text}</span></label>"
        ),
        2 => {
            let pressed = if checked { " aria-pressed=\"true\"" } else { " aria-pressed=\"false\"" };
            format!("<button{data_id} type=\"button\"{pressed}{style_attr}>{text}</button>")
        }
        _ => format!(
            "<label{data_id} class=\"pathland-toggle\"{style_attr}><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"switch\"{checked}><span class=\"pathland-text\">{text}</span></label>"
        ),
