parts.text:
Now render-html: make the COLOR view layout-greedy. In render-html's render_node, the COLOR arm currently:
```rust
component_type::COLOR => {
    let color = node.u32_property(property_id::COLOR, 0xFF00_0000);
    format!("<div{data_id}{event}{aria} style=\"background-color:{};{css}\">{children}</div>", rgba(color))
}
```
Add greedy CSS: `flex:1;align-self:stretch;` — but if WIDTH/HEIGHT set via style_css (css already includes width/height), flex:1 might conflict. To be greedy but respect size: add `flex:1 1 auto;` and `align-self:stretch;`? Actually simplest: prepend `flex:1;` to the style. If WIDTH set, style_css adds `width:...px` which overrides flex-grow effect for that axis (width wins). And cross-axis: `align-self:stretch`. Let me add `flex:1 1 auto;align-self:stretch;` before `background-color`. Since `css` may include width/height/border, ordering: greedy first, then css overrides.

Let me edit the COLOR arm.

