The mount works — "Count: 5" IS emitted at node 9. So the test's `anySetText(frame, "Count: 5")` should find it... but the test failed. Let me look at the test helper:

```java
private static String anySetText(Frame frame) {
    for (Opcode op : frame.opcodes()) {
        if (op.category() == Categories.STYLE && op.command() == Commands.Style.SET_TEXT) {
            return frame.stringAt(op.b());
        }
    }
    return "";
}
```
It returns the FIRST SET_TEXT = "Pathland Kitchensink". Then `anySetText(frame, "Count: 5")` compares `text.equals(anySetText(frame))` → "Pathland Kitchensink".equals("Count: 5") → false!

My helper is wrong — it should check ALL SET_TEXT, not just the first. Let me fix the helper to scan all.

```java
private static boolean anySetText(Frame frame, String text) {
    for (Opcode op : frame.opcodes()) {
        if (op.category() == Categories.STYLE && op.command() == Commands.Style.SET_TEXT) {
            if (text.equals(frame.stringAt(op.b()))) return true;
        }
    }
    return false;
}
```
And for the "Dark: true" contains check:
```java
private static String allSetText(Frame frame) {
    StringBuilder sb = new StringBuilder();
    for (Opcode op : frame.opcodes()) {
        if (op.category() == Categories.STYLE && op.command() == Commands.Style.SET_TEXT) {
            sb.append(frame.stringAt(op.b())).append('\n');
        }
    }
    return sb.toString();
}
```
Then assert `allSetText(frame).contains("Dark: true")`.

Let me fix the test.

