parts.text:
`ng build` succeeds — the templates and TS compile cleanly. 

Now Part 2's remaining piece: the demos' `app.js` (both quarkus and spring). Let me update them:
1. Toggle change handler: `.pathland-toggle` → send VALUE_CHANGED with checked?1:0 (not POINTER_UP).
2. Stepper buttons: `.pathland-stepper button` → read range data-min/max/step + current value span → send VALUE_CHANGED with clamped next value.
3. Picker: `select[data-pathland-id]` change → send VALUE_CHANGED(index).
4. TextEditor: `textarea[data-pathland-id]` input → send TEXT_CHANGED.
5. ColorPicker: `input[type=color][data-pathland-id]` change → send VALUE_CHANGED with packed ARGB bits (need a raw-bits encoder).
6. DatePicker: `input[type=date][data-pathland-id]` change → send DATE_CHANGED (need encoder).
7. SET_TEXT delta: handle textarea (set .value).

Also the SET_PROPERTY delta handler in app.js handles SELECTED (checkbox), VALUE (range). For the new controls, deltas that matter: 
- Toggle SELECTED → checkbox checked (already handled: `input[type=checkbox]`).
- Slider VALUE → range value (already handled).
- Stepper VALUE → the value span text. app.js SET_PROPERTY handler for VALUE only updates `input[type=range]`. Add: update `.pathland-stepper span` text. Let me extend the VALUE prop handler: if el has `input[type=range]` set value; if el is `.pathland-stepper` update its span.
- Gauge/PROGRESS → not crucial for deltas (read-only, no app writes).
- ColorPicker COLOR_VALUE → update input[type=color]. Add handler.
- DatePicker SET_DATE → app.js applyBatch doesn't handle SET_DATE command (style cmd 4). Add: read days → set input[type=date] value. Need date conversion in JS: `new Date(Date.UTC(1970,0,days)).toISOString().slice(0,10)`.
- Picker SELECTION → set select value.
- TextEditor SET_TEXT → textarea value (add to the SET_TEXT handler).

Let me write the new app.js. I'll rewrite both files identically. Let me craft it carefully, reusing existing helpers and adding:
- `CMD_SET_DATE = 4`
- `PROP_SELECTION = 0x2010`, `PROP_COLOR_VALUE = 0x2012`, `PROP_TOGGLE_STYLE`? not needed for deltas.
- `encodeValueBits(target, bits)`
- `encodeDateChanged(target, days, millis)`
- Apply handlers for SET_TEXT (textarea), SET_PROPERTY VALUE (stepper span + range), SELECTION (select), COLOR_VALUE (color input), SET_DATE.
- Event delegation: change handler for `.pathland-toggle` → VALUE_CHANGED 0/1; select; color; date. click handler for `.pathland-stepper button` → compute. input handler for textarea → TEXT_CHANGED. Also text input already handled.

Let me also add a stepper click: read the hidden `.pathland-stepper-range` data-min/max/step, the value span. On click of a button, direction from data-step. Compute next = clamp(current + dir*step). Send VALUE_CHANGED.

Let me write the new app.js (both demos).

Current toggle change handler:
```js
document.addEventListener("change", (event) => {
    const toggle = event.target.closest("label.pathland-toggle[data-pathland-id]");
    if (!toggle || ws.readyState !== WebSocket.OPEN) return;
    const target = Number(toggle.getAttribute("data-pathland-id"));
    ws.send(encodePointerUp(target));
});
```
Change to:
```js
const toggle = event.target.closest("label.pathland-toggle[data-pathland-id]");
if (toggle && ws.readyState === WebSocket.OPEN) {
    const box = toggle.querySelector("input[type=checkbox]");
    ws.send(encodeValueChanged(Number(toggle.getAttribute("data-pathland-id")), box ? (box.checked ? 1 : 0) : 1));
    return;
}
```

Add select/color/date to the change handler:
```js
const select = event.target.closest("select[data-pathland-id]");
if (select && ws.readyState === WebSocket.OPEN) {
    ws.send(encodeValueChanged(Number(select.getAttribute("data-pathland-id")), Number(select.value)));
    return;
}
const color = event.target.closest("input[type=color][data-pathland-id]");
if (color && ws.readyState === WebSocket.OPEN) {
    const rgb = parseInt(color.value.slice(1), 16);
    ws.send(encodeValueBits(Number(color.getAttribute("data-pathland-id")), 0xff000000 | rgb));
    return;
}
const date = event.target.closest("input[type=date][data-pathland-id]");
if (date && ws.readyState === WebSocket.OPEN) {
    if (date.value) {
        const [y, m, d] = date.value.split("-").map(Number);
        const days = Math.round(Date.UTC(y, m - 1, d) / 86400000);
        ws.send(encodeDateChanged(Number(date.getAttribute("data-pathland-id")), days, 0));
    }
    return;
}
```

Click handler add stepper:
```js
document.addEventListener("click", (event) => {
    const button = event.target.closest("button[data-pathland-id]");
    if (button && ...) { ...; return; }
    const stepBtn = event.target.closest(".pathland-stepper button[data-step]");
    if (stepBtn && ws.readyState === WebSocket.OPEN) {
        const stepper = stepBtn.closest(".pathland-stepper[data-pathland-id]");
        if (stepper) {
            const target = Number(stepper.getAttribute("data-pathland-id"));
            const valueEl = stepper.querySelector("span");
            const rangeEl = stepper.querySelector(".pathland-stepper-range");
            const current = Number(valueEl ? valueEl.textContent : 0);
            const dir = Number(stepBtn.getAttribute("data-step"));
            const min = Number(rangeEl.getAttribute("data-min"));
            const max = Number(rangeEl.getAttribute("data-max"));
            const step = Number(rangeEl.getAttribute("data-step"));
            const next = Math.min(max, Math.max(min, current + dir * step));
            ws.send(encodeValueChanged(target, next));
        }
        return;
    }
});
```
Wait — the existing click handler `button[data-pathland-id]` also matches? Stepper buttons don't have data-pathland-id (only the container does). But `.pathland-stepper button[data-step]` selector — `button[data-pathland-id]` won't match stepper buttons. Good. But careful: the original button handler doesn't `return` after send — it just continues. Let me restructure with returns.

Input handler: add textarea:
```js
const textarea = event.target.closest("textarea[data-pathland-id]");
if (textarea && ws.readyState === WebSocket.OPEN) {
    ws.send(encodeTextChanged(Number(textarea.getAttribute("data-pathland-id")), textarea.value));
    return;
}
```
Add BEFORE the `input[type=text]` check (textarea closest won't match input[type=text]).

SET_TEXT handler: add textarea:
```js
const input = el.querySelector("input[type=text]");
if (input) input.value = text;
else {
    const ta = el.querySelector("textarea");
    if (ta) ta.value = text;
    else {
        const span = el.querySelector(".pathland-text");
        if (span) span.textContent = text;
        else el.textContent = text;
    }
}
```

SET_PROPERTY VALUE handler: currently only `input[type=range]`. Extend for stepper span and gauge? For stepper: `el.querySelector(".pathland-stepper span")`? The stepper container has class pathland-stepper; but the span inside. Let me add:
```js
} else if (propId === PROP_VALUE) {
    const el = byId.get(a);
    if (!el) continue;
    const range = el.querySelector("input[type=range]");
    if (range) range.value = String(f32FromBits(c));
    const stepText = el.querySelector(".pathland-stepper span");
    if (stepText) stepText.textContent = String(Math.round(f32FromBits(c) * 100) / 100);
}
```
Hmm the `.pathland-stepper` container el.querySelector("span") would match the first span (the value span). Good.

SET_PROPERTY SELECTION:
```js
} else if (propId === PROP_SELECTION) {
    const el = byId.get(a);
    if (!el) continue;
    const select = el.querySelector("select");
    if (select) select.value = String(c);
}
```
But select IS el (data-pathland-id on select). el.querySelector("select") → null. Use `if (el.tagName === "SELECT") el.value = String(c);`. Let me handle: `const select = el.matches("select") ? el : el.querySelector("select");`.

SET_PROPERTY COLOR_VALUE:
```js
} else if (propId === PROP_COLOR_VALUE) {
    const el = byId.get(a);
    if (!el) continue;
    const color = el.matches("input[type=color]") ? el : el.querySelector("input[type=color]");
    if (color) color.value = "#" + ((c & 0xffffff) | 0x1000000).toString(16).slice(1);
}
```

SET_DATE command (style cmd 4):
```js
} else if (category === CAT_STYLE && command === CMD_SET_DATE) {
    const el = byId.get(a);
    if (!el) continue;
    const date = el.matches("input[type=date]") ? el : el.querySelector("input[type=date]");
    if (date) date.value = c === 0 && b === 0 ? "" : new Date(Date.UTC(1970, 0, b)).toISOString().slice(0, 10);
}
```
Wait — SET_DATE B=days, C=millis. days=20487 → date 2026-02-04. Good.

Encode helpers:
```js
function encodeValueBits(target, bits) {
    // same batch envelope as encodeValueChanged, B = raw bits
    ...
    op.setUint32(8, bits >>> 0, true);
    return out;
}
function encodeDateChanged(target, days, millis) {
    const out = new Uint8Array(16 + 16 + 4);
    ... header ...
    op.setUint8(1, CMD_DATE_CHANGED);
    op.setUint32(8, days >>> 0, true);
    op.setUint32(12, millis >>> 0, true);
    return out;
}
```
CMD_DATE_CHANGED = 13.

Now, both demos' app.js are identical (quarkus META-INF/resources/app.js and spring static/app.js). Let me check the spring one is identical — likely. I'll write the new content to both.

Let me write the full new app.js. I'll construct it carefully.

